:0.0022992597289548528,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":1.1,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.08488767023628031,"_gp_roic_consistency":true,"_score_roic_consistency":85.9,"_gate_incr_roic":0.08209911211760353,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":44.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.04557185965411498,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":48.5,"_gate_pool_share":-0.04315517076557862,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":22.7,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0.061611260602362994,"_gp_fund_growth":true,"_score_fund_growth":61.6,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.030321270195535523,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":44.8,"_gate_share_shrink":0.0028881979481762965,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":46.4,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.003472222222222222,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":94.2,"_gate_insider_own":0.00191,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":1.3,"_gate_insider_buying":0.583,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":58.3,"pf":[],"description_full":"Evergy, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, engages in the generation, transmission, distribution, and sale of electricity in the United States. The company generates electricity through coal, landfill gas, uranium, and natural gas and oil sources, as well as solar, wind, and other renewable sources. It serves residences, commercial firms, industrials, municipalities, and other electric utilities. The company was incorporated in 2017 and is headquartered in Kansas City, Missouri.","ceo_bio":"Mr. David A. Campbell J.D. | CEO, President & Chairman of the Board | Age 57 | Compensation: $2.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 4K people. Revenue per employee of $1.3M ranks in the above the sector median among Utilities peers. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Evergy, Inc. is a large-cap utilities business with a $20.2B market cap on $6.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +1% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 6% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The company is burning through $752M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 5.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 2.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 3.0% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 62% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.6211246814471993},{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.9) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.4% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Utilities peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Regulatory rate-case risk and rising cost of capital \u2014 the allowed return is set by commissions, and the business lives or dies by that negotiation.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Grid modernisation capex burden \u2014 aging infrastructure requires massive reinvestment that regulators may not fully allow into rate base, compressing earned returns.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Wildfire and climate liability \u2014 extreme weather events create catastrophic, uninsurable losses that can push even investment-grade utilities toward restructuring.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Returns on capital have been remarkably steady for 5 years \u2014 durability is the real test of a moat","40 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Utilities sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter","Utilities tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Is Evergy (EVRG) Fully Priced After Raised 2026 Guidance?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/utilities/nasdaq-evrg/evergy/news/is-evergy-evrg-fully-priced-after-raised-2026-guidance","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793942596.986,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.958,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance"]},{"title":"Evergy raises 2026 adjusted EPS guidance to $4.35-$4.50 amid 1.4-gigawatt Digital Realty LOI (NASDAQ:EVRG)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4667665-evergy-raises-2026-adjusted-eps-guidance-to-4_35-4_50-amid-1_4-gigawatt-digital-realty-loi","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793932621.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.382,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"Evergy Inc (EVRG) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Highlights: Raised Guidance, Dividend Hike and a 1. ...","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets